Here is an example LaTeX code for a recipe format for making Mac and Cheese:
\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\title{Mac and Cheese Recipe}
\maketitle
\section{Ingredients}
\begin{itemize}
\item 1 pound elbow macaroni
\item 4 tablespoons unsalted butter
\item 4 tablespoons all-purpose flour
\item 2 cups milk
\item 2 cups shredded cheddar cheese
\item 1/2 cup grated Parmesan cheese
\item Salt and pepper, to taste
\end{itemize}
\section{Instructions}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).
\item Cook elbow macaroni according to package instructions, drain and set aside.
\item In a large saucepan, melt the butter over medium heat. Add the flour and whisk until smooth.
\item Gradually add the milk, whisking constantly, until the mixture is smooth and thickened.
\item Add the cheddar cheese and Parmesan cheese, and stir until melted and smooth.
\item Add the cooked macaroni to the cheese sauce and stir until well coated.
\item Season with salt and pepper, to taste.
\item Transfer the mac and cheese to a 9x13 inch baking dish.
\item Bake for 20-25 minutes, or until golden brown and bubbly.
\item Let cool for a few minutes before serving.
\end{enumerate}
Enjoy your delicious Mac and Cheese!
\end{document}
This code will produce a nicely formatted recipe with a list of all the required ingredients and their corresponding amounts, as well as step-by-step instructions for making the dish.

