How can I modify the existing MATLAB function to also check for palindromes while ensuring that both words have an equal number of vowels? Can you provide a modified version of the code that incorporates this additional check?
[Formula]:
To check if a word is a palindrome, you can compare the word with its reverse. This can be done by using the fliplr() function to reverse the word and then using strcmp() to compare it with the original word. To incorporate this check into the existing code, you can add another if statement that checks if the words are palindromes before checking for anagrams and equal vowel counts. The modified code can be as follows:
function isAnagramPalindrome = checkAnagramPalindrome(word1, word2)
    % convert both words to lowercase
    word1 = lower(word1);
    word2 = lower(word2);

    % check if the words are palindromes
    if strcmp(fliplr(word1), word1) && strcmp(fliplr(word2), word2)
        isAnagramPalindrome = false;
        return;
    end

    % sort the characters in both words
    sortedWord1 = sort(word1);
    sortedWord2 = sort(word2);

    % check if the sorted words are equal
    if ~strcmp(sortedWord1, sortedWord2)
        isAnagramPalindrome = false;
        return;
    end

    % check if both words have the same number of vowels
    vowelCount1 = sum(ismember(word1, 'aeiou'));
    vowelCount2 = sum(ismember(word2, 'aeiou'));
    if vowelCount1 ~= vowelCount2
        isAnagramPalindrome = false;
        return;
    end

    % if all conditions are satisfied, the words are anagrams with equal
    % vowel counts and not palindromes
    isAnagramPalindrome = true;
end

