Can you explain the differences between a Static Web page and a Dynamic Web page using Go code? Please provide examples of each.
A static web page is a web page that is delivered to the user exactly as stored, typically in an HTML file. A dynamic web page, on the other hand, is generated by a web application and the content varies based on user interaction or other factors.
Here is an example of a static web page in Go:
package main
import (
	"fmt"
	"net/http"
)
func main() {
	http.HandleFunc("/", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		fmt.Fprintf(w, "<html><head><title>My Static Page</title></head><body><h1>Welcome to my static page!</h1><p>This is a static web page.</p></body></html>")
	})
	http.ListenAndServe(":8080", nil)
}
And here is an example of a dynamic web page in Go:
package main
import (
	"fmt"
	"net/http"
)
func main() {
	http.HandleFunc("/", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		name := r.FormValue("name")
		if name == "" {
			fmt.Fprintf(w, "<html><head><title>My Dynamic Page</title></head><body><h1>Welcome to my dynamic page!</h1><p>What's your name?</p><form><input type='text' name='name'><input type='submit'></form></body></html>")
		} else {
			fmt.Fprintf(w, "<html><head><title>My Dynamic Page</title></head><body><h1>Welcome, %s!</h1><p>This is a dynamic web page.</p></body></html>", name)
		}
	})
	http.ListenAndServe(":8080", nil)
}
In this example, the user is prompted to enter their name, and the resulting web page is customized based on their input.

